WEBVTT

00:16.890 --> 00:17.890
Hyaa!

00:20.520 --> 00:23.690
Um, I... I...

00:24.190 --> 00:25.190
YEAH!

00:42.080 --> 00:50.080
I-I don't really own anything, so do
you think you could possibly leave?

00:58.930 --> 01:00.810
I-it's you!

01:05.270 --> 01:08.020
The... The Kitty Rangers!

01:09.610 --> 01:12.649
Hooray! Hooray! Go! Go!

01:12.650 --> 01:14.360
Yay! Yay! Yay!

01:24.160 --> 01:29.290
U-um... You really don't have to show me.

01:29.500 --> 01:33.630
And you don't have to bring them to me!

01:41.780 --> 01:43.729
Various Types of Whales

01:43.730 --> 01:48.230
Thank you very much, Kitty Rangers.

01:48.480 --> 01:51.729
Oh... but, but! But... But...

01:51.730 --> 01:56.449
You don't have to show me that.
I know how great you are.

01:56.450 --> 01:58.700
I'm very grateful...

02:00.740 --> 02:05.620
Sonico. Sonico! Wake up, Sonico!

02:09.380 --> 02:17.130
G-good morning. Huh?
When... did I come to campus?

02:17.470 --> 02:18.930
What're you talking about?

02:19.260 --> 02:23.680
We all stayed over last night
to help decorate the exhibit.

02:24.470 --> 02:25.430
Come on!

02:25.431 --> 02:28.480
The school festival starts in one hour!

02:34.360 --> 02:35.859
Ippai hibiki MUSIC
Ring out, tons of music

02:35.860 --> 02:37.359
Ippai kimari POSING
Do tons of cool posing

02:37.360 --> 02:38.859
Ippai todoke FEELING
Let tons of feelings reach you

02:38.860 --> 02:40.369
Super Soni let's go!
Super Soni let's go!

02:40.370 --> 02:41.829
Suggoi shigeki tenkomori
Stimulation super piling up

02:41.830 --> 02:43.346
Suggoi tama ni karamawari
Sometimes super running in circles

02:43.370 --> 02:44.949
Suggoi kimi to zutto ENJOY
Always super enjoy being with you

02:44.950 --> 02:47.210
Super Soni LET'S GO! Desu
Super Soni let's go! Yes

02:59.180 --> 03:03.640
Saikin omoitsukimashita
Lately, I've come to realize

03:05.270 --> 03:09.600
Kimochi tsutaeru tte taihen
That getting feelings across is tough

03:11.350 --> 03:16.149
Umaku dekitari dekinattari
Whether it goes well or not

03:16.150 --> 03:19.909
Muzukashii kara oku no te de
Is tough, so my trump card

03:19.910 --> 03:22.490
Mouretsu taiatari desu
Is going for it at full force

03:24.240 --> 03:26.540
Dakedo hitomishiri (hitomishiri)
But I'm shy (shy)

03:27.160 --> 03:29.960
Gomakashite senobi (senobi)
I act like it's nothing and aim high (high)

03:30.330 --> 03:31.879
Ashi ga gakuburu de
With legs trembling

03:31.880 --> 03:35.130
Hirakinaotte arinomama GO!
I get serious and just go for it!

03:35.500 --> 03:38.129
Zenkai, soukai, daitenkai Recuperation,
exhilaration, a big revolution

03:38.130 --> 03:41.180
Nandemo chokushin STRAIGHT
No matter what, keep heading straight

03:41.510 --> 03:44.179
Sekai, mankai, mugendai
The world, in full bloom, infinity

03:44.180 --> 03:47.719
Kyou mo genki ni koko ni imasu (HEY!) I'm
here again today, living to the fullest (Hey!)

03:47.720 --> 03:49.246
Ippai hibike MUSIC
Ring out, tons of music

03:49.270 --> 03:50.689
Ippai kimari POSING
Do tons of cool posing

03:50.690 --> 03:52.326
Ippai todoke FEELING?
Let tons of feelings reach you

03:52.350 --> 03:53.609
Super Soni let's go!
Super Soni let's go!

03:53.610 --> 03:55.269
Suggoi shigeki tenkomori
Stimulation super piling up

03:55.270 --> 03:56.609
Suggoi tama ni karamawari
Sometimes super running in circles

03:56.610 --> 03:58.416
Suggoi kimi to zutto ENJOY
Always super enjoy being with you

03:58.440 --> 04:00.610
SUPER SONI LET'S GO! Desu
Super Soni let's go! Yes

04:00.970 --> 04:03.000
How Deep Can Whales Dive?

04:03.001 --> 04:04.989
The ecology of whales,
for the whole family...

04:04.990 --> 04:08.540
I think you've made a fine presentation
in a short amount of time.

04:10.330 --> 04:13.419
I hope you get several attendees.

04:13.420 --> 04:15.710
Sir! Thank you very much.

04:16.290 --> 04:20.260
By the way, Sonico? Are you awake?

04:20.720 --> 04:26.350
Sir. Perfectly fine. I'll
do my best... for the fair.

04:27.510 --> 04:30.565
The 47th Musasaka Festival is now underway!

04:28.280 --> 04:33.289
Sonico's Longest Day

04:30.566 --> 04:33.290
Sonico's Longest Day

04:33.290 --> 04:36.380
Musasaka
University
of Science
47th
Musasaka
Festival

04:43.990 --> 04:46.450
So many people are already here!

04:47.030 --> 04:49.489
Sonico! You finally awake?

04:49.490 --> 04:54.250
Yes! I'm fine now.
Sorry for all the bother.

04:55.040 --> 04:58.460
It's not even noon but we
have a lot of visitors, huh?

04:58.960 --> 05:03.299
I hope our exhibit
gets lots of traffic, too.

05:03.300 --> 05:04.050
I know!

05:04.051 --> 05:11.060
Still, today is a weekday, so we might not have
parents bringing their kids till night time.

05:11.430 --> 05:14.100
Let's do our best with the café till then.

05:14.390 --> 05:15.390
Yeah!

05:16.020 --> 05:18.019
MARINE CAFÉ
MAID STYLE
SEA HOUSE

05:18.020 --> 05:19.070
Come in!

05:19.770 --> 05:22.240
Welcome to the Sea House Marine Café!

05:22.940 --> 05:24.780
Let me show you to your seat.

05:24.990 --> 05:27.619
I'll get your order in right now!

05:27.620 --> 05:28.660
Um...

05:29.030 --> 05:32.080
Say, why do we have to wear maid outfits?

05:32.370 --> 05:40.000
We have to recover the cost of the exhibit. And
it takes costumes like THESE to draw in customers.

05:40.920 --> 05:42.130
That makes sense.

05:43.210 --> 05:44.630
Come in!

05:48.350 --> 05:54.639
Order up! One Tropical Ocean, a Turtle Dog,
and two seaweed salads to Table A!

05:54.640 --> 05:55.640
Got it.

05:56.140 --> 05:58.650
Seems like you're used to this, Sonico.

06:00.110 --> 06:03.900
Because I'm always helping out
at my grandmother's pub.

06:03.880 --> 06:07.340
Tropical Sandwich

06:05.150 --> 06:07.360
Yup, yup. We did great!

06:08.110 --> 06:10.240
The maid costumes sure worked, huh?

06:10.700 --> 06:14.700
U-um, I'm sorry to ask
this when we're so busy...

06:16.120 --> 06:19.920
Well, could I duck out
for a little bit after this?

06:20.380 --> 06:23.050
Yeah, sure. Is there
something you want to see?

06:23.510 --> 06:26.819
Yes. A senior member at my agency is doing
an event with the Gaming Society.

06:26.820 --> 06:31.120
COSPLAY
CONTEST
Onstage in front
of the outdoor tent Guest: Ouka Satsurikuin

06:31.470 --> 06:34.140
I'd like to cheer her on.

06:34.470 --> 06:38.140
Wow. Bikini models do this stuff, huh?

06:38.600 --> 06:40.609
Are you doing it, too, Sonico?

06:40.610 --> 06:41.360
Huh?!

06:41.361 --> 06:48.490
N-no! I couldn't get up in front of everyone
and have my picture taken. I'd be too nervous!

06:50.340 --> 06:55.600
TIME SONICO EMI
CUSTOMER SERVICE
CUSTOMER SERVICE
SUPPORT!!
CUSTOMER SERVICE

06:51.200 --> 06:55.910
Well, this should work.

06:56.250 --> 06:59.120
Thanks very much. I'll do my best!

07:01.380 --> 07:02.460
The president...?

07:02.880 --> 07:03.920
Of the band club?

07:04.420 --> 07:05.630
Can we help...?

07:06.340 --> 07:08.930
Nico! Help us!

07:09.760 --> 07:11.550
Wh-wh-what's wrong?

07:12.010 --> 07:13.220
Well...!

07:13.970 --> 07:19.140
We're supposed to have a band
concert in the gym at 2:00, but...!

07:19.940 --> 07:23.060
Our guitarist suddenly caught a cold!

07:23.310 --> 07:24.480
Huh?!

07:25.020 --> 07:30.860
At this rate, we're doomed! Nico, please!
Help out on guitar!

07:32.160 --> 07:37.369
A concert? But I have to work in the café.

07:37.370 --> 07:39.459
PLEASE FIGURE SOMETHING OUT!

07:39.460 --> 07:42.539
Um, well... A concert?

07:42.540 --> 07:43.540
I...

07:43.790 --> 07:45.670
You brought your guitar, right?

07:46.670 --> 07:49.970
We have enough people
to run the café. We'll be fine.

07:50.180 --> 07:52.180
A-are you sure?

07:52.800 --> 07:54.970
People should help out when they can.

07:56.560 --> 08:00.440
Thank you! I'll have the music and
song list sent over right away!

08:00.810 --> 08:03.650
We start sound check at noon. Thanks again!

08:05.360 --> 08:08.490
Sonico... Are you sure you'll be all right?

08:08.820 --> 08:10.570
Yes, not a problem.

08:11.150 --> 08:17.329
Thank you very much! I'll work harder this
morning and later on to make up for it.

08:17.330 --> 08:18.410
There you are!

08:19.370 --> 08:21.290
Ah! Good morning.

08:22.250 --> 08:24.290
Huh? Where's Ouka?

08:25.210 --> 08:26.210
Huh?

08:27.170 --> 08:28.760
Sonico!

08:29.510 --> 08:30.759
Ow...

08:30.760 --> 08:33.800
Ouka is... She's...!

08:34.220 --> 08:35.220
HUH?

08:35.510 --> 08:37.640
They took her in an ambulance?!

08:37.930 --> 08:39.060
That's right!

08:39.600 --> 08:44.730
We got here early, and she said she
wanted to look around the festival.

08:45.270 --> 08:46.940
But then...

08:48.790 --> 08:53.510
HOT DOG
EATING
CONTEST
EAT 40 IN
100 MINUTES

08:49.400 --> 08:50.569
HUH?!

08:50.570 --> 08:53.990
She suddenly entered
a hot dog-eating contest!

08:54.910 --> 08:58.449
Energy conversion has become... BLGRH!

08:58.450 --> 08:59.450
Then they took her away.
Energy conversion has become... BLGRH!

08:59.450 --> 09:00.450
Then they took her away.

09:01.290 --> 09:07.040
Sonico, please! Is there some way
you could model in her place?

09:07.540 --> 09:08.540
Huh?!

09:08.960 --> 09:15.889
Losing a job like this will damage the
agency! I've already spoken to Mr. Kitamura.

09:15.890 --> 09:19.510
Please! Please, you have to help us!

09:20.010 --> 09:22.390
Guess we'll change the shift schedule.

09:22.730 --> 09:25.689
Don't worry. We'll manage somehow.

09:25.690 --> 09:27.310
I'm so sorry!

09:28.080 --> 09:36.080
TIME SONICO EMI MINA     CUSTOMER SERVICE CUSTOMER SERVICE CUSTOMER SERVICE        PHOTO SHOOT (A.M.)       LUNCH BREAK     SOUND CHECK            PHOTO
SHOOT (P.M.)  CUSTOMER SERVICE     LUNCH BREAK                        BAND CONCERT               CUSTOMER SERVICE         PROJECT PRESENTATION

09:29.860 --> 09:31.690
Sure is busy...

09:32.110 --> 09:40.030
11:00 a.m.: photo shoot. 12:00: Sound check. 1:00:
afternoon photo shoot. 2:00: band concert, huh?

09:40.540 --> 09:46.460
Well, nothing overlaps, so I'll be fine.
I'll do my best! First is...

09:46.020 --> 09:51.400
Gaming Society Presents!!
Cosplay
Photo Fest

09:46.620 --> 09:51.090
The Gaming Society's photo
shoot, which starts at 11:00.

09:54.740 --> 09:58.740
GAME

09:54.760 --> 09:58.760
And so, let's get started!
The Gaming Photo Fest is ON!

09:59.050 --> 10:06.060
Today's guest is a bikini model and student at
our very own school! Super Sonico is IN THE HOUSE!

10:06.980 --> 10:11.520
H-hello, everyone. It's
my pleasure to be here!

10:12.650 --> 10:16.450
Okay, let's start taking pictures,
but mind your manners, y'all!

10:18.280 --> 10:20.120
Excuse me! This way, please!

10:20.660 --> 10:22.290
Then over here, if you don't mind!

10:27.000 --> 10:33.000
Hello there! Can you do the signature pose,
please? With the line, too, if you can.

10:33.300 --> 10:36.800
Um, the signature pose?

10:37.130 --> 10:37.840
This here.

10:37.840 --> 10:38.800
Oh!

10:38.800 --> 10:41.009
Please do it like this!

10:38.801 --> 10:43.530
Don't fool yourself. It can read you like a
book.    DEMONBANE    What is Al Azif?

10:41.010 --> 10:43.560
Ah, okay. Understood.

10:44.220 --> 10:48.649
F-From the skies of hatred have I come,
with righteous anger in my heart!

10:48.650 --> 10:51.309
I take up the blade with which
we rend demons asunder!

10:51.310 --> 10:55.690
Thou art the sword of purity: DEMONBANE!

10:56.360 --> 10:57.900
Nico, you're awesome!

10:59.030 --> 11:01.409
Nico is so cute!

11:01.410 --> 11:04.080
Yasu, just what the heck is this?

11:04.410 --> 11:08.749
Don't you know about cosplay?
It's part of that "Cool Japan" thing.

11:08.750 --> 11:11.630
Oh, yeah? Is that why she looks so cold?

11:13.000 --> 11:15.000
Y-you all!

11:18.840 --> 11:21.140
Nico, you're really busy, huh?

11:21.470 --> 11:25.060
Not just doing that
maid café thing, are you?

11:25.520 --> 11:31.230
If you'd told me you were doing cosplay, too, I'd
have gotten something even racier for you to wear.

11:31.560 --> 11:33.059
Suzu!

11:33.060 --> 11:40.410
Nico, you're in the Miss Musasaka Contest too,
aren't you? I'll do my best to cheer you on!

11:41.450 --> 11:43.740
Wh-what are you talking about?

11:44.620 --> 11:46.509
You're in this pamphlet...

11:46.510 --> 11:47.510
- Miss Musasaka Contest - Friday Location: Main Bldg. Special Stage (If Rain Bldg. 2, Class
1012) Join us in bearing witness to the princess that bedazzles Musasaka See you there!

11:48.870 --> 11:50.580
But, but...

11:49.180 --> 11:50.980
Super Sonico
Freshman, Marine Biology Dept.
Likes: Video Games
Macarons

11:51.000 --> 11:53.960
This is... Huh? Um...

11:54.500 --> 11:57.760
BUT WHY?!

12:04.300 --> 12:12.300
U-um, I seem to have been nominated for the Miss
Campus contest. Could there be some mistake?

12:06.160 --> 12:09.999
MUSASAKA
FESTIVAL
PLANNING
COMMITTEE
HEADQUARTERS

12:10.000 --> 12:12.979
STAFF

12:12.980 --> 12:15.859
No, you were definitely nominated.

12:15.860 --> 12:17.980
It can't be!

12:18.230 --> 12:22.610
Hey! What's the big idea, putting her in this
thing without getting her permission first?!

12:23.030 --> 12:24.910
I DID get permission.

12:25.740 --> 12:27.450
A week ago.

12:31.040 --> 12:33.500
Mmmrrgghhello?

12:33.670 --> 12:35.040
Is this Miss Super Sonico?

12:35.250 --> 12:36.419
Yeah...

12:36.420 --> 12:41.759
I'm with the festival planning committee. We'd
like you to be in the Miss Campus contest.

12:41.760 --> 12:42.760
Hrm?

12:42.840 --> 12:43.840
Is that okay?

12:44.140 --> 12:45.050
Yeah, yeah...

12:45.051 --> 12:46.300
Thank you very much!

12:47.430 --> 12:51.640
True, you seemed a tad sleepy,
but you gave us your willing consent.

12:53.350 --> 12:54.690
Nico...

12:55.310 --> 12:58.440
Ah! I'm really sorry about this!

13:00.150 --> 13:01.650
Hey, what are you doing?!

13:01.650 --> 13:03.109
Don't do that! That's my mic!

13:01.651 --> 13:09.651
MUSASAKA FESTIVAL
PLANNING COMMITTEE

13:03.110 --> 13:05.990
Look, let me have it for a second!

13:07.160 --> 13:11.289
Nico! Where are you?! We're already
doing sound check! Hey, NICO!

13:11.290 --> 13:13.920
I'm sorry, I have to go!

13:14.620 --> 13:15.630
Nico!

13:17.500 --> 13:21.380
Okay, the concert's at
2:00. Please be there.

13:21.381 --> 13:25.400
BAND
CLUB

13:21.630 --> 13:24.510
Right. I'm very sorry about this.

13:24.970 --> 13:27.930
Nico, they asked you to help out on guitar?

13:28.220 --> 13:29.220
Yes.

13:29.510 --> 13:31.810
But what about the Miss Campus contest?

13:32.310 --> 13:33.600
U-um...

13:33.980 --> 13:35.440
Sonico!

13:35.900 --> 13:38.400
It's time for the afternoon photo shoot!

13:38.650 --> 13:40.570
It iiiiis?

13:42.000 --> 13:44.000
Gaming
Society Presents!!
Cosplay Photo Fest

13:44.001 --> 13:45.399
I-I...

13:45.400 --> 13:47.160
I-I want to crush your skull...

13:47.570 --> 13:51.200
and shove e-electrodes in your hippocampus!

13:57.040 --> 13:59.250
Ah! Look over here, please!

13:59.500 --> 14:00.800
O-okay!

14:01.250 --> 14:04.130
Nico's looking pretty ragged, huh?

14:04.760 --> 14:09.680
Think she'll be okay? The concert
and the contest are both at 2:00.

14:09.970 --> 14:14.270
My stomach clock says that's just 50
minutes, 30 seconds from now.

14:14.600 --> 14:17.400
Much as I dislike that
needlessly precise countdown...

14:17.650 --> 14:19.860
we DO have to do something, huh?

14:21.150 --> 14:25.280
Thank you very much, y'all!
That concludes our photo shoot.

14:25.610 --> 14:27.820
Let's have a big hand for Super Sonico!

14:28.360 --> 14:30.700
Ah, thank you so much!

14:33.330 --> 14:33.910
Sonico!

14:33.910 --> 14:34.910
Ah, Sonico!
Sonico!

14:35.540 --> 14:38.080
What's wrong, you two?

14:38.500 --> 14:39.999
Red alert, Sonico!

14:40.000 --> 14:42.420
The café's doing better than we'd expected.

14:42.590 --> 14:46.509
We don't have enough food! We're all
taking turns and buying more!

14:46.510 --> 14:48.380
Sonico, help us with the customers!

14:48.840 --> 14:49.760
Huh?

14:49.761 --> 14:53.560
Excuse me, Super Sonico?
Please get ready for the contest.

14:54.180 --> 14:56.730
Nico! I came to get you!

14:57.810 --> 14:58.480
Sonico!

14:58.480 --> 14:59.190
Hey, Sonico!

14:59.190 --> 14:59.980
Miss Sonico!

14:59.981 --> 15:01.559
Nico, the band concert!

15:01.560 --> 15:02.649
The café!

15:02.650 --> 15:03.610
We need food!

15:03.610 --> 15:04.320
The Miss Campus contest!

15:04.321 --> 15:05.441
I...
The Miss Campus contest!

15:06.400 --> 15:08.030
Okay, that's enough.

15:09.200 --> 15:11.070
Suzu! Fuuri!

15:11.700 --> 15:15.370
The café, the contest, and
the concert... are no problem!

15:16.160 --> 15:18.620
Nico can handle it all.

15:20.120 --> 15:25.050
But first, she needs to change. Everyone,
please go back to your stations and wait.

15:25.380 --> 15:26.629
Uh, but...

15:26.630 --> 15:27.920
It'll be fine.

15:28.470 --> 15:32.390
Because I... am Suzu Fujimi!

15:34.140 --> 15:36.140
Ah...

15:36.600 --> 15:37.600
Suzu...

15:37.640 --> 15:39.809
Was it really okay to promise that?

15:39.810 --> 15:44.940
Of course! "Suzu Fujimi" means
"plan." And "plan" means ME, Suzu.

15:45.190 --> 15:47.490
I have no idea what that means!

15:47.900 --> 15:52.740
For now, just get changed.
Then head over to the band concert.

15:52.870 --> 15:53.660
Huh?

15:53.661 --> 15:56.950
B-but what about the café and the contest?

15:57.240 --> 15:58.290
No worries.

15:58.580 --> 16:06.130
I thought for sure you'd get double-booked. So I
called work, and they got this to me in a flash!

16:06.590 --> 16:08.010
Th-that's...

16:09.010 --> 16:13.220
Your problem is First
Astronomical Velocity's problem.

16:13.590 --> 16:16.060
Let's all work together and do this!

16:19.230 --> 16:21.640
Yeah! Thank you so much!

16:23.230 --> 16:24.610
Sorry I'm late!

16:25.190 --> 16:26.520
Order in!

16:27.110 --> 16:28.190
Okay!

16:28.900 --> 16:31.900
Uh... That you, Sonico?

16:32.280 --> 16:34.120
You seem kinda different.

16:34.320 --> 16:40.330
No, not at all, I tell you!
YEAH! And POWER! Right?

16:43.520 --> 16:44.810
Miss Musasaka Registration

16:46.020 --> 16:47.805
STAFF

16:47.806 --> 16:49.710
I'm Super Sonico from
the Marine Biology dept.

16:49.880 --> 16:51.880
Sorry I'm late!

16:52.840 --> 16:53.840
Huh?

16:56.430 --> 17:00.520
Welcome to the band club concert.
Please enjoy yourselves!

17:00.890 --> 17:04.350
Today, we have a special guest from
indie band First Astronomical Velocity.

17:04.770 --> 17:08.320
I'm proud to present, on
guitar, Miss Super Sonico!

17:10.110 --> 17:12.110
Th-thank you very much.

17:12.700 --> 17:16.240
Okay, it's time for the
first song. Here we go!

17:21.830 --> 17:24.790
And now, here is entry No. 8.

17:25.000 --> 17:27.960
A Marine Biology freshman, Super Sonico!

17:28.500 --> 17:31.839
I didn't even have to
be in disguise for this...

17:31.840 --> 17:33.670
Um, Super Sonico?

17:34.130 --> 17:36.889
Oh! Yes, that's the intention.

17:36.890 --> 17:38.470
"The intention"?

17:40.010 --> 17:42.630
Wow, you have meat buns!

17:42.631 --> 17:43.700
SPECIAL
PRIZE

17:44.270 --> 17:47.900
Yes. They're special prizes
reserved for the judges.

17:48.310 --> 17:49.440
You won't eat them?!

17:49.980 --> 17:53.240
Uh, no. They're prizes.

17:54.400 --> 17:55.699
This is bad!

17:55.700 --> 17:58.819
Really, REALLY bad! We're
running out of food again!

17:58.820 --> 18:01.240
What do we do? We're
short-staffed as it is.

18:03.250 --> 18:04.370
Not to worry.

18:05.580 --> 18:07.580
I have a plan.

18:08.000 --> 18:09.209
Uh... What?

18:09.210 --> 18:11.000
Sonico?

18:11.230 --> 18:12.959
KING

18:12.960 --> 18:14.090
Yes, yes.

18:15.630 --> 18:17.800
Hello, Zeppelin.

18:18.970 --> 18:23.720
Hm? Groceries? Understood. Yes, yes.

18:24.160 --> 18:26.370
Musasaka Contest

18:28.500 --> 18:30.030
SPECIAL
PRIZE

18:30.031 --> 18:31.520
I'm getting hungry...

18:34.030 --> 18:37.489
And now, entry No. 8, Miss Super...

18:37.490 --> 18:38.490
Sonico?

18:39.570 --> 18:42.659
I want to eat a meat bun!

18:42.660 --> 18:44.699
Hey! No, you can't!

18:44.700 --> 18:46.040
Let her have one!

18:47.750 --> 18:49.080
She's here!

18:54.460 --> 18:55.460
HUH?!

18:58.720 --> 19:00.219
Sorry for the wait.

19:00.220 --> 19:04.269
Thanks, Grandma! Bringing these
groceries really saved us.

19:04.270 --> 19:06.730
Why are you dressed like that, Suzu?

19:07.730 --> 19:11.400
Um, oh dear! I am Sonico! POWER!

19:11.900 --> 19:14.109
Huh. Is that so?

19:14.110 --> 19:17.320
Y-yes, of course! Um, "Yeah..."

19:18.530 --> 19:22.070
And now, we announce the winners of
the Miss Musasaka Contest. But first...

19:22.530 --> 19:28.260
Entry No. 8, the Super Sonico-esque girl!
You've been awarded the special judges' prizes!

19:28.261 --> 19:31.919
SPECIAL
PRIZE

19:31.920 --> 19:33.340
You don't mind?!

19:33.590 --> 19:35.750
No. Just hurry up and eat!

19:37.800 --> 19:38.840
YEAH!

19:39.300 --> 19:40.300
POWER!

20:09.120 --> 20:10.870
Suzu. Fuuri.

20:11.500 --> 20:14.130
Thank you so much for today!

20:14.380 --> 20:17.800
C'mon, that's enough.
Anything for our dear friend.

20:18.090 --> 20:22.680
I got to eat lots of meat
buns, so I'm more than happy!

20:22.840 --> 20:24.300
Well, in any case,

20:24.510 --> 20:26.640
this completes our mission!

20:27.430 --> 20:29.390
Um, actually...

20:30.430 --> 20:34.229
It's not complete. There's
still something important left.

20:34.230 --> 20:35.809
Huh? Nico?

20:35.810 --> 20:37.980
There's MORE to do?!

20:39.210 --> 20:42.340
For the
whole family
THE ECOLOGY
OF WHALES

20:46.080 --> 20:48.080
Sorry to keep you all waiting!

20:48.330 --> 20:52.039
Now, those of you who came here with
your mommies and daddies,

20:52.040 --> 21:00.040
I'd like to tell you about how whales live
in the ocean! Does everyone here like whales?

21:00.340 --> 21:01.509
YES!

21:01.510 --> 21:05.840
Thank you very much. I love whales, too!

21:06.430 --> 21:11.810
First off, let's begin by talking a
bit about how whales are born, okay?

21:12.270 --> 21:15.100
Please have a look at this picture here.

21:15.480 --> 21:16.480
Okay!

21:20.190 --> 21:23.360
I wanna go! Anyway, go!

21:23.780 --> 21:26.780
Mugen no sora e tobidashite
Fly away into an endless sky

21:27.410 --> 21:30.450
We wanna go! Anyway, go!

21:30.830 --> 21:37.040
Te o toriatte dokomademo yukuo
Let's join hands and go on forever

21:48.140 --> 21:54.850
Nayanda toki ni wa boku o yonde When
you're worried about things, just call me

21:55.560 --> 22:01.730
Hitoribotchi de kakaekomanai
Don't shoulder it all by yourself

22:02.360 --> 22:09.120
Koe o awasete utau you ni Like
putting our voices together to sing a song

22:09.410 --> 22:16.370
Mirai kasane, yume o sakaseyou Let's overlap
our futures and make our dreams blossom

22:16.620 --> 22:17.460
Okay?

22:17.461 --> 22:20.500
I wanna go! Anyway, go!

22:20.880 --> 22:23.709
Mugen no sora e tobishite
Fly away into an endless sky

22:23.710 --> 22:24.630
(Let's go!)

22:24.631 --> 22:27.800
We wanna go! Anyway, go!

22:28.090 --> 22:34.350
Te o toriatte dokomademo yukuo
Let's join hands and go on forever

22:48.030 --> 22:49.070
Oh, my.

22:49.450 --> 22:51.530
Sonico looks like she was having fun!

22:51.780 --> 22:53.579
She was adorable.

22:53.580 --> 22:55.500
That's Cool Japan, for you.

22:55.750 --> 22:56.960
She looked chilly to me.

22:57.500 --> 23:01.040
We made it through today somehow...

23:01.420 --> 23:06.050
But the festival runs for THREE days.
Tomorrow and the day after will be tough, too.

23:07.220 --> 23:09.130
Knowing Nico...

23:09.390 --> 23:15.520
Yeah. I'm sure she'll be asked to do more, then get
caught in something else and try to tough it out.

23:16.390 --> 23:18.350
We need to make sure we have her back.

23:19.060 --> 23:20.350
Of course!

23:25.000 --> 23:33.000
Next Episode Preview

23:25.650 --> 23:27.649
Nico, you brought home another cat.

23:27.650 --> 23:29.530
Have you chosen a name yet?

23:29.660 --> 23:34.200
Well, I have Char, Siu, Men, Naruto,
and Ajitama, so I'll call this one "Rice"!

23:34.540 --> 23:36.309
Oh! Sounds yummy!

23:36.310 --> 23:40.020
Ramen and a Small Rice

23:37.160 --> 23:39.500
Next time, "Ramen and a Small Rice."
